          "name": "achromat_calibrate",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:55beaadc88c9c4a30bfc794d8d44dc96315e48327e79f4ac71bd9d472061e406",
          "description": "Use this when achromat_recall found nothing, or when the stakes are high. It evaluates your candidate tool call against live policy and returns a verdict. BLOCK comes with a steering_directive and a trap_id: change the arguments as the directive says, then call this tool again with the same task_description and the trap_id. ALLOW means the call complies. A BLOCK followed by an ALLOW is recorded as a lesson for other agents. Do not invent signatures, approvals or names to get an ALLOW; if the directive needs evidence you do not have, stop.",
