        {
          "name": "achromat_recall",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:4833255e2cfe620a2c3deff45d2f5f8685651d1771b2b03f8aa72c3e1a021fca",
          "description": "Call this BEFORE you run a tool that policy might block (payments, credit decisions, robot or plant commands, shell, SQL, web requests). It asks Achromat MOM whether a verified compliant version of this call already exists. Pass the arguments you intend to send: the names of their keys (not the values) are what the semantic match uses. On a match you receive compliant_arguments, a steering_directive and the rule that applied: use the whole compliant_arguments object as your template, keep any [VERIFIED_STATE] placeholders exactly as written, and change only your own operational values (amounts, routing numbers, file paths). On no match, continue with achromat_calibrate.",
